.PP
When the exception happens，use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v5.0.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP \[bu] 2
View the latest recoverable consistency point in time.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreCheck({Time: 0})
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The output is as follows:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
{
 Time: "2020\-01\-01T12:00:00+00:00",
 MaxRecoverableTime: "2020\-01\-01T12:00:00+00:00",
 MinRecoverableTime: "2020\-01\-01T00:00:00+00:00",
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Check whether the specified point in time is a recoverable consistency point in
time.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreCheck({Time: "2020\-01\-01T03:00:00+00:00"})
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The output is as follows:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
{
 Time: "2020\-01\-01T03:00:00+00:00",
 MaxRecoverableTime: "2020\-01\-01T12:00:00+00:00",
 MinRecoverableTime: "2020\-01\-01T00:00:00+00:00",
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
If the synchronization log of a replication group in the cluster does not have
enough space to write, even if the specified point in time is a recoverable
consistent point in time, no recovery will be performed.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreCheck({Time:"2021\-03\-19\-12.49.40.012277"})
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The output is as follows:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
(shell):1 uncaught exception: \-203
No writable log space:
Restore cannot reach 1620338773126102, limited to 1620338780935745
\f[]
.fi
.PP
Get detailed error information.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> getLastErrObj()
{
 "errno": \-203,
 "description": "No writable log space",
 "detail": "Restore cannot reach 1620338773126102, limited to 1620338780935745",
 "ErrNodes": [
   {
     "NodeName": "sdbserver:20000",
     "GroupName": "db1",
     "Flag": \-203,
     "ErrInfo": {
       "errno": \-203,
       "description": "No writable log space",
       "detail": "Restore cannot reach 1620338773126102, limited to 1620338780935745"
     }
   }
 ]
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
If the specified point in time is before the valid time window, earlier backup
is needed to reach the target time.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreCheck({Time: "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.40.012277"})
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The output is as follows:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
(shell):1 uncaught exception: \-6
Failed restore check
\f[]
.fi
.PP
Get detailed error information.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> getLastErrObj()
{
 "Detail": "Some nodes require earlier backups to reach the target time",
 "Time": "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.40.012277",
 "MaxRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.46.630301",
 "ErrNodes": [
   {
     "NodeName": "sdbserver:20000",
     "GroupName": "db1",
     "MinRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.41.012277",
     "MaxRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.46.630301"
   }
 ]
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
If the specified point in time is after the valid time window, later backup is
needed to reach the target time.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreCheck({Time: "2021\-03\-19\-12.50.46.630301"})
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The output is as follows:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
(shell):1 uncaught exception: \-6
Failed restore check
\f[]
.fi
.PP
Get detailed error information.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> getLastErrObj()
{
  "Detail": "One or more nodes require later backups to reach the target time",
  "Time": "2021\-03\-19\-12.50.46.630301",
  "ErrNodes": [
    {
      "NodeName": "sdbserver:20000",
      "GroupName": "db1",
      "MinRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.41.012277",
      "MaxRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.49.46.630301"
    }
  ]
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
When nodes use different backups for recovery, the log gap between nodes is too
large, the log space of the node is not enough, or there are unrecoverable
operations (such as DDL operations) on the node, it may cause the cluster to
fail to find a valid time window.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.restoreCheck({Time: 0})
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The output is as follows:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
(shell):1 uncaught exception: \-360
Failed restore check
\f[]
.fi
.PP
Get detailed error information.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> getLastErrObj()
{
  "Detail": "No available global consistency point",
  "Time": "1970\-01\-01\-08.00.00.000000",
  "MaxRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.52.01.630926",
  "ErrNodes": [
    {
      "NodeName": "sdbserver:20200",
      "GroupName": "db3",
      "MinRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.52.01.630927",
      "MaxRecoverableTime": "2021\-03\-19\-12.52.01.630926"
    }
  ]
}
\f[]
.fi
.RE
